[{"section":"why-splicing","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-1\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-1-title splice-fig-1-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 230\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-1-title\">RNA precursor and spliced product</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-1-desc\">Exons E1, E2 and E3 are retained in order; intervening RNA I1 and I2 is excised. The chromosome is unchanged.</desc><text x=\"320\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Pre-mRNA (5′ → 3′)</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"42\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"218\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">I1</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"42\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E2</text><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"475\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"423\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">I2</text><rect x=\"475\" y=\"42\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"525\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E3</text><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M320 121 L315.29581493962405 113.32727930146444 L324.70418506037595 113.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"107\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Splicing</text><rect x=\"170\" y=\"135\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"135\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E2</text><rect x=\"370\" y=\"135\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"420\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E3</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"193\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Mature exon-containing RNA</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">New exon junctions; original exon order retained</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 1. Exons E1, E2 and E3 are retained in order; intervening RNA I1 and I2 is excised. The chromosome is unchanged.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-1\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"split-gene-evidence","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-2\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-2-title splice-fig-2-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 220\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-2-title\">Hybridization evidence for interrupted genes</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-2-desc\">A mature RNA pairs with separated complementary DNA regions. DNA that corresponds to an excised intron remains unpaired in a conceptual hybrid.</desc><text x=\"35\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">DNA</text><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"420\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M220 65 C220 5 420 5 420 65\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" /><text x=\"320\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Unpaired DNA</text><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"420\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M220 100 L420 100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">RNA</text><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"425\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"107\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"107\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"442\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"442\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"459\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"459\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"141\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"141\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"476\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"476\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"158\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"158\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"493\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"493\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"175\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"510\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"192\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"192\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"527\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"527\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"209\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"209\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"544\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"544\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"320\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Dotted RNA segment represents joined retained regions in a schematic</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"178\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\">The loop is evidence of discontinuous correspondence</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Not by itself proof of the catalytic mechanism</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 2. A mature RNA pairs with separated complementary DNA regions. DNA that corresponds to an excised intron remains unpaired in a conceptual hybrid.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-2\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"signals","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-3\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-3-title splice-fig-3-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-3-title\">Typical major-class intron landmarks</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-3-desc\">Donor GU, branch A, polypyrimidine tract and acceptor AG cooperate in recognition. Vertical boundaries mark the exchanged phosphates.</desc><rect x=\"28\" y=\"72\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"88\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><rect x=\"515\" y=\"72\" width=\"100\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"565\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E2</text><text x=\"153\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">GU</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A</text><text x=\"423\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">UUCUU</text><text x=\"493\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">AG</text><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M128 54 L123.29581493962407 46.32727930146445 L132.70418506037592 46.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M515 54 L510.29581493962405 46.32727930146445 L519.704185060376 46.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"128\" y=\"21\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">5′ donor</text><text x=\"515\" y=\"21\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">3′ acceptor</text><line x1=\"345\" y1=\"129\" x2=\"345\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M345 94 L349.70418506037595 101.67272069853556 L340.29581493962405 101.67272069853556 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Branch point</text><line x1=\"423\" y1=\"129\" x2=\"423\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M423 94 L427.70418506037595 101.67272069853556 L418.29581493962405 101.67272069853556 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"455\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Pyrimidine tract</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">5′</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">3′</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 3. Donor GU, branch A, polypyrimidine tract and acceptor AG cooperate in recognition. Vertical boundaries mark the exchanged phosphates.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-3\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"snrnps","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-4\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-4-title splice-fig-4-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 235\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-4-title\">Early and late donor recognition</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-4-desc\">U1 first pairs with the donor; during activation the site is transferred into the U6-containing catalytic organization.</desc><text x=\"320\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Early recognition</text><rect x=\"42\" y=\"47\" width=\"110\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"68\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><line x1=\"152\" y1=\"63\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"63\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"200\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">donor</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"89\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">U1</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"89\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"185\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"89\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"205\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"89\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M320 150 L315.29581493962405 142.32727930146444 L324.70418506037595 142.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"367\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Activation</text><rect x=\"42\" y=\"161\" width=\"110\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><line x1=\"152\" y1=\"177\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"177\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><rect x=\"150\" y=\"189\" width=\"120\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">U6</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"177\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"189\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"185\" y1=\"177\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"189\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"205\" y1=\"177\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"189\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"452\" y=\"204\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">U1 has departed</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 4. U1 first pairs with the donor; during activation the site is transferred into the U6-containing catalytic organization.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-4\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"snrnps","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-5\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-5-title splice-fig-5-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 210\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-5-title\">Bulged branch nucleotide</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-5-desc\">A simplified U2–precursor pairing diagram leaves the internal branch A unpaired, exposing its 2′ hydroxyl for the first reaction.</desc><text x=\"30\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Pre-mRNA</text><path d=\"M120 65 L280 65 Q320 8 360 65 L520 65\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" /><text x=\"320\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"43\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">2′-OH</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"520\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"129\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">U2</text><line x1=\"135\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"405\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"405\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"185\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"430\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"455\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"455\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"235\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"480\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"505\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"505\" y2=\"121\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"53\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M320 53 L325.43037744428045 60.177116469213104 L316.0668991252217 61.095104539709055 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"179\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Branch A is positioned, not buried in a duplex</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 5. A simplified U2–precursor pairing diagram leaves the internal branch A unpaired, exposing its 2′ hydroxyl for the first reaction.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-5\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"assembly","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-6\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-6-title splice-fig-6-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 245\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-6-title\">Major spliceosome assembly</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-6-desc\">Early recognition E, stable U2 recruitment A, tri-snRNP association B, activation with departure of U1 and U4, followed by chemistry and release.</desc><rect x=\"25\" y=\"34\" width=\"125\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"87.5\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E: U1 + factors</text><rect x=\"185\" y=\"34\" width=\"120\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A: + U2</text><rect x=\"340\" y=\"34\" width=\"145\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"412.5\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">B: + tri-snRNP</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M185 58 L177.32727930146444 62.704185060375934 L177.32727930146444 53.295814939624066 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"305\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M340 58 L332.32727930146444 62.704185060375934 L332.32727930146444 53.295814939624066 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"412\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"122\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M412 122 L407.29581493962405 114.32727930146444 L416.70418506037595 114.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"330\" y=\"122\" width=\"165\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"412.5\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Activated: U2/U6/U5</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">U1, U4 leave</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"286\" y2=\"146\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M286 146 L293.67272069853556 141.29581493962408 L293.67272069853556 150.70418506037592 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"132\" y=\"122\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Step 1 → Step 2</text><line x1=\"132\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"146\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M100 146 L107.67272069853556 141.29581493962408 L107.67272069853556 150.70418506037592 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"122\" width=\"76\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"62\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Release</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"209\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">ATP-dependent rearrangements occur between assembly states</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Phosphotransfer uses the precursor's existing phosphates</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 6. Early recognition E, stable U2 recruitment A, tri-snRNP association B, activation with departure of U1 and U4, followed by chemistry and release.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-6\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"phosphotransfer","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-7\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-7-title splice-fig-7-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 215\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-7-title\">Two boundary phosphates</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-7-desc\">P1 at the donor becomes the branch phosphate; P2 at the acceptor becomes the normal exon junction. Both originally belong to the precursor.</desc><rect x=\"35\" y=\"48\" width=\"125\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"97.5\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"64\" r=\"16\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">P1</text><line x1=\"196\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"435\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><circle cx=\"455\" cy=\"64\" r=\"16\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"455\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">P2</text><rect x=\"475\" y=\"48\" width=\"125\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"537.5\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E2</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Intron</text><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M180 125 L175.29581493962408 117.32727930146444 L184.70418506037592 117.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><line x1=\"455\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"455\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" /><path d=\"M455 125 L450.29581493962405 117.32727930146444 L459.70418506037595 117.32727930146444 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"128\" width=\"200\" height=\"45\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"155.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">2′–5′ branch bond</text><rect x=\"355\" y=\"128\" width=\"200\" height=\"45\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--surface)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"455\" y=\"155.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">3′–5′ exon bond</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">The two phosphorus centers are conserved through the exchanges</text></svg><figcaption>Figure 7. P1 at the donor becomes the branch phosphate; P2 at the acceptor becomes the normal exon junction. Both originally belong to the precursor.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"splice-fig-7\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"},{"section":"first-step","html":"<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg id=\"splice-fig-8\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"splice-fig-8-title splice-fig-8-desc\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 245\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"var(--ink)\"><title id=\"splice-fig-8-title\">First transesterification</title><desc id=\"splice-fig-8-desc\">Branch A 2′-OH attacks the donor phosphate, producing free E1 3′-OH and a lariat intron still joined to E2.</desc><rect x=\"25\" y=\"36\" width=\"110\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"var(--panel)\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">E1</text><circle cx=\"154\" cy=\"52\" r=\"13\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">P</text